{"page_content": "A.16-2.4.2.2. Exposure in water/sediment compartments\n\nThe exposure in water takes into account both release via drift (for spraying application only) and runoff and accounts for degradation of the substance in water. The surface water is represented by a ditch surrounding a 1 hectare field (1:10 surface ratio between field and water), with a depth of 30 cm and where the residence time of water is 40 d (Table R.16-8). The exposure estimation of the surface water concentration (to be used in the risk assessment) is as follows:\n\n1. The concentration in surface water is calculated for each day during 365 days (not an average) taking into account the releases from drift (when applicable) and runoff, as indicated above, dilution in the water body and removal processes in water:", "metadata": {"doc_id": "0796c742-9bc6-49bf-a80a-74521cf8c94b", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}